<KickoffSession
    documentTitle="Resilience as the baseline. | Canada2080"
    description="Dr Michael Donaldson on architecture, local infrastructure, and a founding story at the Canada2080 kickoff."
    eyebrow="Capacity · 1:55 p.m."
    headline="Resilience as the baseline."
    name="Dr Michael Donaldson"
    bio="Dr Michael Donaldson is Principal Architect and Designer at DWA / Future Workshop. His practice spans architecture, strategic design, and designed futures."
    profileUrl="https://www.designworkshop.ca/studio"
    profileLabel="Design Workshop"
    podiumSrc="/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5425.jpg"
    podiumAlt="Dr Michael Donaldson speaking at the podium, in a white shirt and white glasses."
    photos={[
        {
            src: "/images/events/2026-kickoff/gallery/img_5425.jpg",
            alt: "Dr Michael Donaldson speaking at the podium, in a white shirt and white glasses.",
            caption: "At the podium.",
        },
    ]}
>
    <p class="lede">
        An innovation mindset, in his usage, is an unwillingness to accept what
        is not working, and the habit of encouraging that unwillingness.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            The largest holders of commercial property and infrastructure
            capital, he said, still want a six-month return from assets that
            mature over 10 to 20 years.
        </li>
        <li>
            His test: four days in the depth of winter, the power out, and no
            food coming in. Would a city know what to do?
        </li>
        <li>
            He argued for decentralized local infrastructure, and for resilience
            as a baseline expectation rather than an add-on.
        </li>
        <li>
            Private practice, he said, shows systems that deliver little of what
            they promise. Architects and citizens should stop accepting
            processes that do not work.
        </li>
        <li>
            Both of his parents volunteered at Expo 67. He asked for a founding
            story strong enough to rally a resilient economy, rather than being
            absorbed into someone else's.
        </li>
    </ul>
</KickoffSession>
